Source: obsidian
Section: editors
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Ackerman-00 <noreply@example.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), desktop-file-utils, zlib1g, zlib1g-dev
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Rules-Requires-Root: no
Homepage: https://obsidian.md/

Package: obsidian
Architecture: amd64
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, bash, hicolor-icon-theme, libasound2t64, libatk1.0-0t64, libatk-bridge2.0-0t64, libatspi2.0-0, libayatana-appindicator3-1, libcairo2, libcups2t64, libdbus-1-3, libdbus-glib-1-2, libdbusmenu-glib4, libexpat1, libfontconfig1, libgbm1, libgcc-s1, libgdk-pixbuf-2.0-0, libglib2.0-0t64, libgtk-3-0t64, libnotify4, libnspr4, libnss3, libpango-1.0-0, libpipewire-0.3-0t64, libpulse0, libsecret-1-0, libstdc++6, libudev1, libx11-6, libxcb1, libxcomposite1, libxdamage1, libxext6, libxfixes3, libxkbcommon0, libxrandr2, xdg-utils
Description: A powerful knowledge base for plain text Markdown files
 Obsidian is a powerful knowledge base that works on top of a local folder
 of plain text Markdown files.
